--TEST--
Core\Ldap::open asks `ldap.open` about the URL's host before anything is resolved, so a host outside the grant throws `RuntimeError` — ADR 0278 § 2 and `rule:security/capability-question-is-grant-and-scope`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `ldap.open` grants hosts under `example.test`, and this host is not one.
try {
    var $other = Core\Ldap::open({url: "ldaps://directory.example.net"});
    echo "opened", "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    echo $refused->message, "\n";
}

// `*.example.test` matches at a label boundary, so the bare domain is not granted.
try {
    var $bare = Core\Ldap::open({url: "ldaps://example.test"});
    echo "opened", "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $refused) {
    echo $refused->message, "\n";
}
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.ldap]
open = ["*.example.test"]
--EXPECT--
Core\Ldap::open needs the capability `ldap.open` for directory.example.net, which is not granted
help: grant it in nvs.toml under `[capabilities.ldap]`
Core\Ldap::open needs the capability `ldap.open` for example.test, which is not granted
help: grant it in nvs.toml under `[capabilities.ldap]`
